LAST_SHIPPED='1H bets on NFL & CFB (2026-09-19, Josh: "1H bets should be included on NFL & CFB"): the three first-half markets (h2h_h1, spreads_h1, totals_h1) ride the existing per-event props pull on both leagues (CFB_PROPS_ODDS_MARKETS and both feeds.oddsPropMarkets end with them; no new pull, no budget/reserve/slot/plan change, +3 nominal credits per priced event only when a book returns the half). src/lib/cfb/markets.ts is the vocabulary (ml_1h/spread_1h/total_1h, isH1Market, baseMarketOf, marketWord, H1_SIGMA_SCALE = 1/sqrt 2); src/lib/cfb/h1.ts holds parseH1 (the full game'"'"'s readBooksOf under the half'"'"'s sigma, same Pinnacle-weighted median, pHome = ML + spread-implied blend with no FPI term) and attachH1 (joins the stored set onto the slate by ESPN id, up to six rows per game through the same sideRow that prices full-game sides). Stored under <board prefix><date>:h1 (propsStore.readH1/writeH1, written by football-props.ts after the board, carried like stored prop rows); both slate routes read it. Surfaces: Board categories 1H ML / 1H SPREAD / 1H TOTAL + three parlay sets (13 pregame categories), every-pick list, ranked chips, game card + sandbox grid 1H rows with the half-time score, slip/ticket wording, Sharp "1H lines" pill; one leg per market per game counts the half with the full game. Grading on ESPN'"'"'s half-time score (linescores periods 1+2 -> homeH1/awayH1/h1Final, finals[id].h1) the moment the half is over, even while live; full-game legs byte-identical. The auto paper card stays FULL-GAME only (Josh'"'"'s call). The splits feed has no 1H sides.'
